    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good summary. but when you say it \"ironically\" leads to stagnation, it sounds like you're saying the negative side is more likely the real-world outcome. based on the economic data, is there actually a way to balance the two, or is the consensus pretty much that any extra regulation just ends up being a net loss for the economy?",
